           $$$$$$$$$$ Help string $$$$$$$$$$$
"Enabling this parameter allows local logic to override normal output behavior in the event of a Network Fault.  Network Faults include, Duplicate MacId failure and Module Bus Off conditions.  The default is Disabled.  For more details, consult the product documentation.",
0,1,0,                     $ Min, Max (max enumeration #), and Default values
,,,,,,,,,,,;               $ Not Used

$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$
Param28 =                  $ Comm Status Override
0,                         $ reserved
7,                         $ Link Path Size
"21 0F 00 24 0E 30 01",    $ Link Path to param instance.
0x0002,                    $ No support for settable path, scaling, scaling links,
                           $ or real time update of value.  Value is gettable and
                           $ Settable.  Enumerated strings are supported.
0xC1,                      $ Data Type - boolean
1,                         $ Data Size - (in bytes)
"Comm Status Override",    $ Parameter Name
"",                        $ Units String
           $$$$$$$$$$ Help string $$$$$$$$$$$
"Enabling this parameter allows local logic to override normal output behavior in the event of a Communication Status change.  These events include all states where the module is without an I/O connection in the run state.  This can happen if the I/O connection does not exist, has timed out, has been deleted, or is currently idle.  The default is Disabled.  For more details, consult the product documentation.",
0,1,0,                     $ Min, Max (max enumeration #), and Default values
,,,,,,,,,,,;               $ Not Used




